top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">UK Prime Minister Andy Burnham is visiting Berlin to launch a new bilateral treaty and hold talks with Chancellor Friedrich Merz. President Steinmeier is on a state visit to France. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea warns of AI-aided hacking after bank data breaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:343f70c3850c92f3001d34758ffa0de8712206dfc9342177b5d07b4de9f69f1f</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:44:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T12:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922--3290ee11faa1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seoul is alarmed after a recent breach of South Korean banks' cyber defenses that reportedly involved AI-assisted hacking. Officials warn such methods could be used to also target other sectors and government agencies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Opposition doubles down against poll chief after detentions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96c6ad6b7aa14102568e52f2ea88f1e4c46a204c32e7beb8568b70975fec5a9d</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:43:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T12:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-doubles-down-against-poll-chief-after-detentions/live-79587554--49a24ea9d897.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-doubles-down-against-poll-chief-after-detentions/live-79587554?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's opposition alliance is gearing up for another day of protests after demonstrating lawmakers were detained for the second time. Meanwhile, India is seeking to repatriate its nationals working in Russian military.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Security in the Black Sea region: is Bulgaria the weak link in Europe's defense against threats from Russia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:520b23831357fc5f80d7b5041e8b6c5217646051cb1313978247634683117f78</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:44:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/security-in-the-black-sea-region-is-bulgaria-the-weak-link-in-europe-s-defense-against-threats-from-/a-79592663--cd93d129d2db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/security-in-the-black-sea-region-is-bulgaria-the-weak-link-in-europe-s-defense-against-threats-from-russia/a-79592663?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two ships have sunk off the coast of Bulgaria and Romania after drone attacks in recent days. Bulgaria has held back on pointing the finger at Russia. What does that mean for security in the Black Sea and the region?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>French police arrest 5 suspects over Renoir museum theft</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b896f6e2ccf2b8174009e3e962c29d8b1d31e6e92adb8d3b850b042b30cdd97a</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:44:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/french-police-arrest-5-suspects-over-renoir-museum-theft/a-79595309--449b653fc5c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/french-police-arrest-5-suspects-over-renoir-museum-theft/a-79595309?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Thieves broke into the Renoir Museum on the French Riviera last month and made off with two paintings. The heist follows a string of high-profile robberies from European museums.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How a multibillion-dollar oilfield has ignited the UK-Argentina feud over the Falklands</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b073d5660abccd98609041b69839f1f2eadd391fa630bcd1313b348fbf716332</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:44:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-a-multibillion-dollar-oilfield-has-ignited-the-uk-argentina-feud-over-the-falklands/a-79588973--b9ae4084dbb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-a-multibillion-dollar-oilfield-has-ignited-the-uk-argentina-feud-over-the-falklands/a-79588973?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Argentina and the UK once fought a war over the Falkland Islands. Now, the multibillion-dollar Sea Lion oil project has reignited old tensions, with Buenos Aires seeking to put a stop to the plans.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Prize in literature goes to Canada's Anne Carson</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4880724b209d6bb84629b857d0f40bbe1f99205c3dcc8ccb02b286c751027646</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:44:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T11:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-goes-to-canada-s-anne-carson/a-79594136--7b591c2af8dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-prize-in-literature-goes-to-canada-s-anne-carson/a-79594136?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Carson won for her "bold and inventive oeuvre." The decorated poet and essayist is known for her reverence for Latin and Greek classics.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea recalls Ukraine ambassador amid POW dispute</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64143abfbf39b81ecd896359c4066862852068ec3e14541c198f1508544bfb9d</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:44:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-recalls-ukraine-ambassador-amid-pow-dispute/a-79590511--9732a38bcd21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-recalls-ukraine-ambassador-amid-pow-dispute/a-79590511?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Korea has said it will recall its ambassador to Ukraine. Seoul is upset about a transfer of North Korean prisoners of war being made public knowledge at the UN and had demanded — but not received — an apology.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As Russia steps up attacks on Ukrainian data centers, could Ukraine soon be offline?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d282d05115bd5a81450cd249c729095314ea58daf6ac6da448e7b4b0142bab9d</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:45:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-data-centers-could-ukraine-soon-be-offline/a-79582503--ed9380350022.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-russia-steps-up-attacks-on-ukrainian-data-centers-could-ukraine-soon-be-offline/a-79582503?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russia targets Ukraine's data centers more and more, experts say the country's internet system is too robust to shut down entirely. However, services could become more expensive.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine says 30 killed, 18 wounded in Russian attack on passenger buses in Kramatorsk</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6df5d218530c5dd7d2b6b167c0f962c53627d0da7e43cda2c74046c9835732cc</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:45:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-says-30-killed-18-wounded-in-russian-attack-on-passenger-buses-in-kramatorsk/a-79592331--68b467e629df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-says-30-killed-18-wounded-in-russian-attack-on-passenger-buses-in-kramatorsk/a-79592331?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities in the eastern Ukrainian city of Kramatorsk have suspended public transport following the deadly attack near the front line.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK scales back Jerusalem consulate after Israel dispute</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:209f87d461fa0f79b6a78b6520e11779ca987b609c82add915bc7d541be9d27c</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:45:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T09:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-scales-back-jerusalem-consulate-after-israel-dispute/a-79590790--0207c62f89a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-scales-back-jerusalem-consulate-after-israel-dispute/a-79590790?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Britain says its diplomatic mission will remain open with reduced staff, despite Israel's order to close the nearly 200-year-old consulate.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German Bundeswehr: A new naval port in Emden aims to enhance Germany's defense capabilities</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:408ac83d65a2ca0600a7245523177f61c3cde1ea9fc961c30e57a0875d71dd71</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:45:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T09:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-bundeswehr-a-new-naval-port-in-emden-aims-to-enhance-germany-s-defense-capabilities/a-79561414--c280e8efd5f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-bundeswehr-a-new-naval-port-in-emden-aims-to-enhance-germany-s-defense-capabilities/a-79561414?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Citing the escalating security threat, Germany's Navy has decided to establish a second port on the North Sea coast. Emden was chosen as the location.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>NASA Apollo program pioneer Margaret Hamilton dies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39593c4e27396ac5659e5e8e7108cfd36c8cec2c372ffb8f335190be43ed86c5</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:45:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T09:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nasa-apollo-program-pioneer-margaret-hamilton-dies/a-79589778--947538374c2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nasa-apollo-program-pioneer-margaret-hamilton-dies/a-79589778?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US scientist Margaret Hamilton is being hailed as a pioneer for her groundbreaking work developing software for NASA's Apollo lunar program. She died at the age of 90.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Middle Corridor: Can Bulgaria be a safe gateway for Asian imports to the EU?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13ec9ae0049f56134961c0b3aaae9766d33fa17dea2db0f76e7d2208c58d79de</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:45:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T08:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/middle-corridor-can-bulgaria-be-a-safe-gateway-for-asian-imports-to-the-eu/a-79584530--0deecfdaf02f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/middle-corridor-can-bulgaria-be-a-safe-gateway-for-asian-imports-to-the-eu/a-79584530?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU wants more trade via the Middle Corridor, which could bring big benefits for Bulgaria. But Tuesday's drone attacks on commercial ships off the Bulgarian coast are a stark reminder of the security risks involved.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US to lay fresh torture charges against Venezuela's Maduro and wife</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6e176047fbbf923dc42b4f5e52bb5154cfebe3494949670cdc472440e5a39e9</id><updated>2026-10-08T15:45:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T06:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-to-lay-fresh-torture-charges-against-venezuela-s-maduro-and-wife/a-79588019--d71ec6f0f716.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-to-lay-fresh-torture-charges-against-venezuela-s-maduro-and-wife/a-79588019?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">